State which plugin copy is answering, and put LOADING inside the language box

A run reported "4/4 workers" with 8 configured, and no code path that reads the setting was wrong -
so the settings page now states the facts needed to see why: the worker count in force against the
configured one, the assembly the plugin was loaded from, and the settings file it reads. The
startup log carries the same three, so a second loaded copy (an older plugin folder that survived
an update, each holding its own configuration) is visible instead of silent.

The language box also says LOADING inside itself now - same box, same position, the text swapped
and restored - rather than drawing a layer over the text that was already there.

Version 1.1.0.37.
